WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
Together compiler delivers up to 2.6 times higher throughput for variable load inference without manual retuning. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 225. OpenAI's new image models and Google's gray area classifiers come next. Then the agent papers, things to try, on the horizon, and under the hood. Together AI, Mark Tech Post reports, ship together compiler as an agent-driven loop that keeps rewriting the inference forward pass as traffic moves.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.600
It topped the strongest inference X setups in under 24 hours per model.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.780
Optimization is handled as continual compilation instead of a single static pass, with light

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:44.060
agents watching token throughput and rewriting kernels live.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:50.200
The method stays model agnostic on existing checkpoints, an open source compiler loop code

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:55.080
is coming with integration guides for VLLM and tensorRTLLM back ends.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:02.636
Images 2.6 landed with GPT image 2.6 flair and sunburst application programming interface,

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.276
or API models.

00:01:04.916 --> 00:01:07.756
Flair generates images in as little as six seconds.

00:01:08.296 --> 00:01:14.776
Both models add GIF output, scalable vector graphics, or SVG, export, markup edits, and

00:01:14.776 --> 00:01:20.096
a complexity parameter, aimed at visual assets inside agent loops and design tools that

00:01:20.096 --> 00:01:21.236
need faster iteration.

00:01:21.236 --> 00:01:27.036
Google Research released Agile Deliberation, a human-in-the-loop setup that lets users

00:01:27.036 --> 00:01:30.176
define fuzzy visual concepts from borderline images.

00:01:30.796 --> 00:01:37.336
Across 18 live sessions, it lifted Gemini-based Classifier F1 by 10.5 points over 0 shot.

00:01:38.076 --> 00:01:43.096
Ambiguous examples go to human adjudication instead of locking a binary label too soon.

00:01:44.132 --> 00:01:50.012
SRM, on Archive, jointly evaluates targeted retrieval and global reconstruction on synthetic

00:01:50.012 --> 00:01:59.572
sets of 10 to 100 factual statements. QN 2.5 at 1.5 billion parameters reached 86.7% retrieval accuracy,

00:02:00.112 --> 00:02:09.612
and 45.7% reconstruction, while the 3 billion variant scored 72.2% and 18.5%. Reconstruction fell

00:02:09.612 --> 00:02:15.612
faster than retrieval as context grew, so retrieval only scores mismemory loss in small models.

00:02:15.612 --> 00:02:21.854
Base is a belief-aware critic that tracks epistemic status on top of a frozen large language

00:02:21.854 --> 00:02:27.414
model, or LLM. It chooses how many clarifying questions to ask more consistently than

00:02:27.414 --> 00:02:33.894
GRPO or Archer on the SimMC 2.1 reference game. The method records how many questions each

00:02:33.894 --> 00:02:40.273
ambiguous reference needs and penalizes premature answers. ProMemory separates maintaining future

00:02:40.273 --> 00:02:45.493
intentions from deciding when to realize them. It keeps pending objectives with supporting evidence.

00:02:45.493 --> 00:02:51.273
Check new observations against activation conditions and update state after actions complete.

00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:56.253
Delayed intention and open-ended assistance benchmarks showed consistent gains across

00:02:56.253 --> 00:03:00.533
multiple LLM backbones while limiting unnecessary interventions.

00:03:01.557 --> 00:03:07.437
Search-equipped agents got a stage-resolved cognitive bias analysis that logged queries, retrieved

00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:09.717
documents, openings, and final answers.

00:03:10.277 --> 00:03:14.217
The run covered 10 models across 1,000 synthetic search worlds.

00:03:14.217 --> 00:03:19.237
Final answers were more sensitive to initial evidence order during active search than when

00:03:19.237 --> 00:03:24.257
all evidence arrived at once, and dead end histories reduced strategy switching beyond

00:03:24.257 --> 00:03:27.196
what context length alone predicts.

00:03:27.236 --> 00:03:33.816
EditVito sits a 0.6 billion-parameter gate after a full context LLM rewrite of optical character

00:03:33.816 --> 00:03:38.496
recognition, or OCR output, and keeps or reverts each line block.

00:03:38.496 --> 00:03:45.996
The gate improved all five rewriters tested on Hype OC Repair 2026, cutting weighted character

00:03:45.996 --> 00:03:54.816
match error rate or CMARR by 0.0026 to 0.0044. It works on rewriters unseen during training

00:03:54.816 --> 00:04:02.060
and raises preference scores by 0.15 to 0.25. Fine-tuning a re-ranker on the answer each

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:07.480
evidence set produces, plus a small comparison head is how rag-compice routes retrievers.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:13.460
sensors. Answer F1 rose 28% relative to the best fixed retriever, and most of that gain

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:19.340
held under unseen corpora, retrievers, or readers. The router reads passage sets directly,

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:25.844
so it is not stuck with query-only features. Geometry-aware regularization is the idea behind

00:04:25.844 --> 00:04:31.684
G-Edit, which uses a low-rank plus diagonal factor model to protect a core-knowledge subspace

00:04:31.684 --> 00:04:38.784
while loosening constraints on hard edits. On GPTJ and LLMA-38 billion, it beat baselines on both

00:04:38.784 --> 00:04:45.024
editing success and knowledge preservation across up to 10,000 sequential updates, with no retraining

00:04:45.024 --> 00:04:52.002
of the base model. On archive, CCD Wiki encodes clinical hypotheses as mutable entries bound to

00:04:52.002 --> 00:04:58.182
corroborating and contradicting evidence, so longitudinal cognitive behavioral therapy, or CBT,

00:04:58.182 --> 00:05:01.582
state's evidence grounded without backbone retraining.

00:05:02.062 --> 00:05:08.222
Remaining expert renormalization or unnormalized rerouting produces the lowest perplexity only

00:05:08.222 --> 00:05:12.882
when the inference time expert deactivation rule matches the training time weight rule

00:05:13.142 --> 00:05:18.842
and mismatches inflate perplexity 14 fold to 28,740 fold.

00:05:19.282 --> 00:05:25.402
Consultation value distillation estimates human consultation value offline via Monte Carlo

00:05:25.402 --> 00:05:30.582
rollouts and distills it into lightweight predictors that improve budgeted allocation across batch

00:05:30.582 --> 00:05:36.682
and sequential settings. Tandem Bench contains 1,200 multi-agent cooking questions,

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:43.742
where the best native decision model reaches 62.50% accuracy, while optimality verification

00:05:43.742 --> 00:05:52.362
stays near chance. Cart Bench supplies 1,328 expert annotated criteria across 17 retail domains,

00:05:52.362 --> 00:06:00.782
and three of 10 evaluated models exceed 90% on core criteria, while none exceeds 45% on excellence criteria.

00:06:01.462 --> 00:06:09.102
A knowledge graph audit using an error rate times FanOutQ leaves 3.98 to 4.74 percentage points more errors

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:13.702
than a joint model with identical actions on held out redock red graphs.

00:06:14.162 --> 00:06:20.142
Under deployable conditions, a learned conversational emotion shift model beats the predicted label baseline

00:06:20.142 --> 00:06:26.042
