More labs will publish agent harness compliance audits that follow the banking rule study pattern.

00:14:44.301 --> 00:14:50.721
Additional multilingual factuality benchmarks modeled on NIJA facts are likely for other low resource regions.

00:14:51.779 --> 00:14:58.419
Let me pop the hood on recurrent depth, where Hawk and Griffin match Lama II after training on six times fewer tokens.

00:14:58.419 --> 00:15:04.419
The design reuses the same transformer layers in a loop instead of stacking new ones, so

00:15:04.419 --> 00:15:08.339
a small model gets more sequential compute steps without extra parameters.

00:15:08.979 --> 00:15:14.019
Each layer receives the current token representation, and a recurrent state carried from its own

00:15:14.019 --> 00:15:18.659
previous pass, the mechanism laid out in the block recurrent transformer paper.

00:15:19.599 --> 00:15:24.099
Complexity stays linear in sequence length, and the model can still refine its internal

00:15:24.099 --> 00:15:26.439
state over multiple iterations at inference.

00:15:26.439 --> 00:15:32.519
size, or initialize that recurrent state carelessly, and the model loses the ability to extrapolate

00:15:32.519 --> 00:15:33.699
beyond training lengths.

00:15:34.319 --> 00:15:40.439
Relaxed recursive transformers add depth-wise low-rank adaptation, or Laura, modules that

00:15:40.439 --> 00:15:45.659
loosen strict parameter sharing and recover most of the original accuracy at roughly one-quarter

00:15:45.659 --> 00:15:46.659
the parameter count.

00:15:47.219 --> 00:15:52.699
Recurrent Gemma's 2 billion and 9 billion variants reach downstream scores comparable to standard

00:15:52.699 --> 00:15:58.119
Gemma checkpoints, despite fewer training tokens, and they run with fixed memory cost on

00:15:58.119 --> 00:15:58.919
long sequences.

00:15:59.619 --> 00:16:02.959
Use recurrent depth when parameters or tokens are the bottleneck.

00:16:03.359 --> 00:16:07.719
Keep a deeper feed forward stack when you need the best single pass on short context.

